  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Frank about tea production in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tea, after water is world&#x2019;s most consumed beverage. Frank About Tea created a supply chain skipping the tea auction and any middlemen, which resulted in a tea supply chain that is 6 times shorter. Not only is the tea fresher and the quality higher, but there is also complete transparency from harvest to product. Tea leaves are to be processed within 7 hours after harvesting them. Frank About Tea imports high quality tea from Kenya through direct trade. To further develop towards the demand for premium, high quality tea, DGGF-TA funded a feasibility study for the creation of a climate neutral production and packaging factory in Kenya or Uganda. This feasibility study will show how to proceed, a likely outcome is to further develop an existing factory, make it climate neutral and include packaging processes within the same facility.</narrative>
  </description>
